<http://data.silknow.org/object/9c7f26c7-262e-39ba-a4b0-5c4cf7a722bb>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Middle East, Textile;"@en , "silk satin and metal thread bordered with silk damask brocaded with metal thread, backed with block-printed cotton and faced with plain weave silk.\nThe dark blue satin ground of the main panel is woven with red, yellow and green silk and metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a silk core] with regular rows of short, right-leaning botehs.\nBorder: pieced orange silk damask brocaded with metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a silk core] in a floral bouquet.  The damask sub-pattern is floral sprays and a stylised leaf-shape in a zigzag pattern. As the border is pieced from a long length, the repeating nature of the brocaded motifs is indistinct.\nBacking: pieced; plain weave white cotton block printed with red, yellow and blue with tightly scrolling stems bearing radiating flower heads.\nFacing: bias cut green silk which appears on the front only as a narrow band."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/20d5d715-ce21-3dbf-8480-2780f0b2d5cd> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f7fe7921-2410-3481-864d-fcfb66baedcc> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "silk satin and metal thread bordered with silk damask brocaded with metal thread, backed with block-printed cotton and faced with plain weave silk.\nThe dark blue satin ground of the main panel is woven with red, yellow and green silk and metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a silk core] with regular rows of short, right-leaning botehs.\nBorder: pieced orange silk damask brocaded with metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a silk core] in a floral bouquet.  The damask sub-pattern is floral sprays and a stylised leaf-shape in a zigzag pattern. As the border is pieced from a long length, the repeating nature of the brocaded motifs is indistinct.\nBacking: pieced; plain weave white cotton block printed with red, yellow and blue with tightly scrolling stems bearing radiating flower heads.\nFacing: bias cut green silk which appears on the front only as a narrow band."@en , "Middle East, Textile;"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/9c7f26c7-262e-39ba-a4b0-5c4cf7a722bb/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/9c7f26c7-262e-39ba-a4b0-5c4cf7a722bb/dimension/2> ;
